The audience is first-time, never-licensed applicants for a Michigan operator's license, reading at a plain-English level, plus newcomers and parents of teen drivers who use the same handbook. This section covers Graduated Driver Licensing for teens under eighteen, the driver education segments, the Level One, Level Two and Level Three licenses with their restrictions, adults who were never licensed, and the identity, legal presence and residency documents. It teaches the order of driver education segments and license levels, the supervised driving and restriction rules a teen must follow, and what documents every first-time applicant brings. It assumes no prior driving knowledge and no prerequisites beyond literacy, so wording stays concrete, procedural and free of legal jargon throughout.
